Spec: Course entity and course view

Purpose:
  The Course entity (name and display color) and the classic per-course calendar, one row per calendar week and one
  column per weekday.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py
  ./view.py
  ./routes.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  ../lessons/lessons.sdd
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd
  ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd

Must:
  A Course has a name and a display color used for lesson squares.
  @CourseRepository in ./ports.py exposes list, get and add operations backing ./services.py.
  Each row of the course view is one calendar week and columns are days of the week.
  Lessons and holidays are shown on their day cell, read through ../lessons/lessons.sdd and
  ../holidays/holidays.sdd services rather than their repositories directly.
  For the admin, clicking a day cell opens the dialog specified in ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd.

Tasks:
  [?] Decide whether the view shows one selected course, all courses, or a date range, and how the user navigates
  [ ] Implement @Course, @CourseRepository and the SQLite adapter
  [ ] Implement the weekly grid in ./view.py and ./routes.py
